  product="forest-shuffle-insert"
  publishDate="2026-11-20"
>
  <p>
    Both are nature games about building an engine: Wingspan fills three habitats with birds, Forest
    Shuffle surrounds trees with animals and plants. They often get recommended together, and they feel
    quite different once you play them. Here's how they compare.
  </p>

  <KeyTakeaway answer="Pick Wingspan if you want a full board game with dice, eggs and four rounds that build to a big finish, or if you mostly play solo, since its Automa is in the box. Pick Forest Shuffle if you want something quicker to teach, mostly cards, and tight at two players. If you already own Wingspan, Forest Shuffle is different enough to earn its shelf space." />

